      "problem": "Find the midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(-w,7z)$ and $(5w,-3z).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(-w,7z)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(5w,-3z)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z+(-3z)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-w+5w}{2},\\frac{7z-3z}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4w}{2},\\frac{4z}{2}) \\\\  & =(2w,2z).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
